atlas optimization-readiness

architecture readiness-state
  canonical_name ReadinessState
  owns ReadinessLabel
  owns AdmissionLadder
  owns DependencyEdge
  consumes Capability
  consumes BodyAvailability
  consumes CarrierAdmission
  publishes ReadinessLabel
  publishes ExecutableFrontier
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Readiness
  layer governance
  semantic_question Can this be executed right now, and if not, exactly which rung of the ladder is missing?
  purpose Make readiness impossible to confuse with architectural completeness. A target shape may be arbitrarily large; the executable frontier is whatever needs nothing else. Every element carries a label and, when blocked, names the single dependency that blocks it.
  maturity architectural
  node_types ReadinessLabel
  node_types AdmissionRung
  node_types Dependency
  node_types ExecutableFrontier
  edge_types blocked_by
  edge_types unlocks
  edge_types measured_by
  invariant every element of the map carries exactly one readiness label
  invariant a blocked element names the dependency that blocks it, not a general condition
  invariant a large target shape is never evidence of progress; only MEASURED is
  invariant an unmeasured claim is labelled CANDIDATE regardless of how well specified it is
  invariant a derived metric is not a proven fact; a promoted conclusion keeps its provenance, its measurement universe and its verification state
  invariant an audit's own output is not source truth
  invariant a prior conclusion, including one produced by this system, is re-verifiable and never a frozen invariant
  forbidden_inference a well-specified abstraction -> an executable one
  forbidden_inference breadth of the target map -> readiness
  forbidden_inference a capability being described -> a body existing
  forbidden_inference a body existing -> a service running
  forbidden_inference a service running -> this carrier reaching it
  forbidden_inference a prior Bonfyre conclusion -> a verified fact
  interacts optimization-proof
  interacts preservation-boundary
  interacts compression-law
  source_lineage Generation-10 readiness separation, 2026-08-26
  source_lineage four observed capability-versus-reachability failures, 2026-08-26

label MEASURED
  detail A number exists, taken over a named universe, at a named revision.
label EXECUTABLE
  detail Needs nothing that does not already exist. On the frontier.
label BLOCKED_BY
  detail Fully specified and waiting on exactly one named dependency.
label DECLARED
  detail The namespace or contract exists; nothing populates or implements it.
label CANDIDATE
  detail Proposed. No commitment, no dependency analysis, no measurement.

rung r1-capability
  question Can this semantically be done?
rung r2-body-availability
  question Does an implementation or body exist?
rung r3-service-availability
  question Is that body actually running?
rung r4-carrier-admission
  question Can this carrier reach it?
rung r5-authority-admission
  question May this caller use it?
rung r6-execution-admission
  question Is it executable now?
  detail The conjunction of every rung above.

ladder_invariant a failure is localized to one rung and reported as that rung
ladder_invariant no rung implies any rung below it
ladder_example a compiled route set with no serving host is r1 yes, r2 yes, r3 no, and therefore r6 no
ladder_example a working command-line path whose protocol wrapper fails is r1 yes, r2 yes, r3 yes, r4 no
ladder_note reporting the whole as unavailable when only one rung is missing hides the cheapest available fix

interaction readiness-labels-every-claim
  source readiness-state
  destination optimization-proof
  relation labelling_constraint
  preserves the separation between a specified abstraction and an executed one
  drops any presentation in which described, blocked and measured elements appear at equal maturity
  forbidden_inference an item appearing in a capability map -> that item being actionable

architecture analysis-universe
  canonical_name AnalysisUniverse
  owns ObservedSet
  owns UniverseDigest
  consumes SubjectClosure
  publishes ObservedSet
  publishes UniverseCompatibility
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Measurement identity
  layer governance
  semantic_question Under what conditions was this set observed, and is another set lawfully comparable to it?
  purpose Stop counts and finding sets from being treated as timeless facts. Every observed set carries the universe that produced it, and a comparison across universes requires explicit reconciliation rather than subtraction.
  maturity architectural
  node_types AnalysisUniverse
  node_types ObservedSet
  node_types UniverseReconciliation
  edge_types observed_under
  edge_types comparable_to
  invariant an observed set carries a universe digest covering subject closure, revision, inclusion and exclusion rules, tool, tool version, configuration and environment
  invariant two sets are comparable only under the same universe digest, or through an explicit reconciliation that states what differs
  invariant a count without a universe is a number, not a measurement
  invariant divergent inclusion rules between a local run and a scheduled run make the two sets incomparable until reconciled
  forbidden_inference two counts of the same kind -> those counts being comparable
  forbidden_inference a finding disappearing between runs -> that finding being resolved
  forbidden_inference a smaller set -> improvement
  interacts readiness-state
  interacts optimization-proof
  applies_to static analysis findings
  applies_to test results
  applies_to benchmark and performance measurements
  applies_to security scans
  applies_to route and source censuses
  applies_to model evaluations
  applies_to compression measurements
  applies_to observation scrapes
  source_lineage Generation-10 readiness separation, 2026-08-26

architecture independent-oracle
  canonical_name IndependentOracle
  owns ComparisonContract
  owns ArbitrationContract
  owns ResidualClass
  consumes SubjectClosure
  consumes ObservedSet
  publishes Residual
  publishes DispositionVerdict
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Independent recomputation
  layer governance
  semantic_question When two realizations of the same calculation disagree, which one is operative, and what would it take to overturn it?
  purpose Make independent recomputation usable against a live financial system. Without an arbitration rule the first run produces residuals nobody can triage, and trust in the mechanism dies immediately.
  maturity architectural
  node_types OperativeRealization
  node_types AdvisoryRealization
  node_types Residual
  node_types ResidualClass
  node_types ArbitrationContract
  edge_types compared_against
  edge_types classified_as
  edge_types corroborated_by
  invariant exactly one realization is operative; every other is advisory
  invariant a residual is evidence, never a verdict
  invariant a residual alone never alters financial state, never relabels the operative result as wrong, and never triggers automatic repair
  invariant the operative result stands until a residual is independently corroborated
  invariant the comparison contract declares rounding, ordering, grouping, null semantics and effective-date semantics before the first run, not after the first argument
  invariant a disagreement is classified before it is escalated
  forbidden_inference a difference -> a defect
  forbidden_inference an advisory realization being newer or cleaner -> it being correct
  forbidden_inference agreement between two realizations sharing an assumption -> independent corroboration
  interacts readiness-state
  interacts preservation-boundary
  source_lineage Generation-10 readiness separation, 2026-08-26

residual_class ORACLE_SCHEMA_MISREAD
residual_class ORACLE_MISSING_BUSINESS_RULE
residual_class ROUNDING_CONVENTION_DIFFERENCE
residual_class ORDERING_ONLY
residual_class REPRESENTATION_ONLY
residual_class HISTORICAL_LEGACY_QUIRK
residual_class LEGACY_SUSPECTED_DEFECT
residual_class LEGACY_CONFIRMED_DEFECT
residual_class ORACLE_CONFIRMED_DEFECT
residual_class AMBIGUOUS

corroboration_route independent corroboration by a third realization
corroboration_route historical output evidence
corroboration_route domain or human confirmation
corroboration_route a reproduction from first principles against source records

agreement_topology two_agree_one_differs
  detail When the operative and one advisory agree and a second advisory differs, the differing advisory's interpretation is suspect before the operative result is.
agreement_topology operative_alone
  detail When both advisories agree against the operative, the operative becomes a substantially stronger defect candidate, though still not confirmed.
agreement_topology all_differ
  detail When every realization differs, the comparison contract is probably incomplete; fix the contract before raising any defect.
agreement_topology all_agree
  detail Strong evidence, and the only cheap outcome.
